WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.294 --> 00:00:04.713
The real way to make a
difference --

00:00:05.339 --> 00:00:07.049
Sheila:
5-6-7-8, to the Right!

00:00:07.049 --> 00:00:09.134
♪♪

00:00:09.134 --> 00:00:10.636
-- is to make a fortune.

00:00:10.636 --> 00:00:11.637
♪♪

00:00:11.637 --> 00:00:16.350
Rose:
Physical is southern California,
1980's, aerobics, big hair,

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:18.769
bad marriage. The dawn of a new
day.

00:00:18.769 --> 00:00:21.355
Are you finally ready to make that
campaign video?

00:00:21.355 --> 00:00:22.898
I'm ready to make a fortune.

00:00:22.898 --> 00:00:24.358
♪♪

00:00:24.358 --> 00:00:27.694
When we meet Sheila, she is at a
very dark moment

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:28.737
Annie:
in her emotional life.

00:00:28.737 --> 00:00:30.822
Annie:
She's been in the shadows of a

00:00:30.822 --> 00:00:33.242
Annie:
really dynamic and charismatic
husband.

00:00:33.242 --> 00:00:37.579
And there's this seed inside
her that wants more than that.

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:38.997
Babe, we all gotta do our
part.

00:00:38.997 --> 00:00:40.165
Are you getting signatures?

00:00:40.165 --> 00:00:42.000
No, I'm the candidate.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.587
Sheila and Danny, both
individually want something
more.

00:00:45.587 --> 00:00:47.547
Rory:
Danny wants to become a
politician,

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:51.843
Rory:
Sheila is trying to claim her
independence in society.

00:00:51.843 --> 00:00:54.137
For her it's about ownership,
it's about independence.

00:00:54.137 --> 00:00:57.099
Rose:
Sheila is a unique
heroine because she's an anti-heroine really.

00:00:57.099 --> 00:00:59.017
Whose side are you on?

00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:00.018
I'm on my side.

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:04.356
Annie:
Sheila's suffering from body
dysmorphia and bulimia.

00:01:04.356 --> 00:01:07.025
And that causes all kinds of
fallout in her life.

00:01:07.025 --> 00:01:10.028
Rose:
A big part of Sheila's story is
her illness

00:01:10.028 --> 00:01:10.737
Rose: 
with food.

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:14.241
And it's an illness that women
have that women don't talk about,
a lot.

00:01:14.241 --> 00:01:17.452
I struggled with eating
disorders through much of my
life.

00:01:17.452 --> 00:01:22.374
Annie:
So I wanted to explore how
divided women often feel projecting

00:01:22.374 --> 00:01:26.920
Annie:
a certain look and personality
on the outside, but having

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:30.215
Annie:
something much darker and
secretive on the inside.

00:01:30.215 --> 00:01:34.344
Everybody has inner voices that
we try to temper, and with
Sheila,

00:01:34.344 --> 00:01:35.470
Rose:
you get kind of this insight

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:36.305
and I love that.

00:01:36.305 --> 00:01:38.765
Sheila:
(You're short, round, lumpy,
nobody wants you)

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:39.599
Stop it!

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:44.313
It's such a great, unique
perspective on how women talk to
themselves.

00:01:44.313 --> 00:01:46.565
Dierdre:
And the complexity of female
friendships.

00:01:46.565 --> 00:01:49.318
Yeah you weren't listening to me
because I'm a boring fat
housewife, who's like why do you....

00:01:49.318 --> 00:01:51.737
-No, no, no, don't say that, you
look great.

00:01:51.737 --> 00:01:53.447
Oh that, thank you. It's a new
dress.

00:01:53.447 --> 00:01:54.948
I'm sorry this class is full.

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:57.034
There's plenty of space back
here.

00:01:57.034 --> 00:01:59.119
With Sheila and Bunny...

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:01.455
Della:
I both hate her and want to
destroy her, 

00:02:01.455 --> 00:02:04.833
but I also really want to be her
friend and love her. (Laughs)

00:02:04.833 --> 00:02:06.793
Della:
So...It's about these
dualities.

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:08.420
You have to press power.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:09.171
Thanks.

00:02:09.171 --> 00:02:10.839
(Click)
♪♪

00:02:10.839 --> 00:02:12.883
It's like the contrast of these
two sides of her.

00:02:12.883 --> 00:02:15.218
Rose:
It's the life of Sheila and her
domestic life.

00:02:15.218 --> 00:02:16.845
Putting on a face for everybody
and then

00:02:16.845 --> 00:02:19.348
the life of her discovering
aerobics.

00:02:19.348 --> 00:02:20.974
♪♪

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:24.478
Sheila:
It's special, and it makes me
feel...powerful.

00:02:24.478 --> 00:02:25.479
♪♪

00:02:25.479 --> 00:02:28.398
Her idea to have women
find power

00:02:28.398 --> 00:02:32.277
Annie:
through physical strength,
that's the revolution that she's enacting.

00:02:32.277 --> 00:02:35.781
I ate a batch of oatmeal cookies
one by one while the sun came
up.

00:02:35.781 --> 00:02:38.408
You can't do anything about that
but you can change this moment.

00:02:38.408 --> 00:02:39.868
Right now...if you move.

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:41.161
♪♪

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:43.288
We tried to really take aerobics
seriously

00:02:43.288 --> 00:02:45.791
Annie:
and show what it did to empower
women in the 80's.

00:02:45.791 --> 00:02:49.294
Every ugly thought you've ever
had about yourself, let it fuel
you!

00:02:49.294 --> 00:02:51.797
Punch, punch, punch,
punch, punch, punch, punch!

00:02:51.797 --> 00:02:56.843
Annie:
The way that we dramatize this
power inside Sheila,

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:59.471
is through this really dynamic
movement of the camera.

00:02:59.471 --> 00:03:01.598
There's this momentum that
starts to happen

00:03:01.598 --> 00:03:04.810
as she escalates into this high
that she gets from aerobics.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:06.228
That becomes her passion.

00:03:06.228 --> 00:03:07.479
♪♪

00:03:07.479 --> 00:03:12.234
Craig Gillespie, who directed
the pilot had this very strong
vision.

00:03:12.234 --> 00:03:15.237
The creative design of this has
been so collaborative

00:03:15.237 --> 00:03:17.406
Dierdre:
in terms of establishing 1981.

00:03:17.406 --> 00:03:19.533
Such an interesting time in
fashion

00:03:19.533 --> 00:03:22.035
because it's just coming out of
the 70's into the 80's.

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:23.328
Rose:
So it's a really sweet spot.

00:03:23.328 --> 00:03:25.664
I remember first trying on the
wig and and going "I can't

00:03:25.664 --> 00:03:28.667
wear this" and then by the end
I'm like "Bigger, bigger, 
bigger!"
(Laughing)

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:31.461
On my God, you look amazing.

00:03:31.461 --> 00:03:33.422
So do you, those colors.

00:03:33.422 --> 00:03:35.966
Rory:
I mean getting dressed up in
clothes from 1981

00:03:35.966 --> 00:03:39.428
and have my hair look like this
is wildly fascinating to me.

00:03:39.428 --> 00:03:43.723
Rory: But to have it be 10
episodes of a show that are very
entertaining

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:46.601
Rory:
and actually about something
meaningful is awesome.

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:48.728
I couldn't had done any of this
without you, you know that
right?

00:03:49.938 --> 00:03:52.732
Annie:
I can't talk about this show
anymore without talking about Rose.

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:55.944
She's surpassed any expectation
I could've had.

00:03:55.944 --> 00:03:57.654
Annie:
She doesn't hold anything back.

00:03:57.654 --> 00:03:58.530
♪♪

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:00.031
Rose:
We didn't want to pull any
punches.

00:04:00.031 --> 00:04:02.576
Rose:
And that's what makes the show
interesting and a bit dangerous.

00:04:02.576 --> 00:04:07.706
♪♪

00:04:07.706 --> 00:04:09.249
Let's do this thing!

